## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to enforce cross-provider tagging policy across environments using plan JSON, with CI gating and explicit drift handling.

## Key Concepts
- plan JSON parsing across AWS and GCP
- per-env backends and state isolation
- gating deployments behind approvals
- drift detection via re-plan and re-validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js validator skeleton
const plan = require('./plan.json');
let ok = true;
(plan.resource_changes || []).forEach(r => {
  const tags = (r.change?.after?.tags) || {};
  if (!tags.CostCenter || !tags.Env) ok = false;
});
process.exit(ok ? 0 : 1);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would policy checks adapt to Terraform Cloud/Enterprise?
- How handle resources with dynamic tags or provider-specific nuances?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests multi-account Terraform patterns: provider aliases, cross-account data sources, and deterministic apply order.

## Key Concepts

- Aliased providers
- Cross-account data sources
- Data referencing across providers
- depends_on for ordering
- Credentials management via profiles and assume_role

## Code Example

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  alias   = "prod"
  region  = "us-east-1"
  profile = "prod"
}
provider "aws" {
  alias   = "audit"
  region  = "us-east-1"
  profile = "audit"
}

data "aws_caller_identity" "prod" {
  provider = aws.prod
}

data "aws_s3_bucket" "prod_bucket" {
  provider = aws.prod
  bucket   = "my-prod-bucket"
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "audit" {
  provider = aws.audit
  statement {
    actions   = ["s3:GetObject"]
    resources = ["${data.aws_s3_bucket.prod_bucket.arn}/*"]
    principals {
      type        = "AWS"
      identifiers = ["arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.prod.account_id}:root"]
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "audit_bucket" {
  provider = aws.audit
  bucket   = "audit-bucket"
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "audit_policy" {
  provider = aws.audit
  name     = "CrossAccountGetObject"
  policy   = data.aws_iam_policy_document.audit.json
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate credentials for the aliased providers safely?
- How would you test this cross-account permission in a CI workflow?
